WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.640
Look inside any proton or any neutron,
and you will find three quarks.

2
00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.700
And only two kinds of quark
are needed: up and down.

3
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.580
Yet the proton carries
a charge of plus one,

4
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.440
while the neutron
carries no charge at all.

5
00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.140
Same two ingredients, different result.

6
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.760
So why is only one of them charged?

7
00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:24.330
In this mission, you'll
build baryons quark by quark,

8
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.850
including antimatter versions
such as the antiproton.

9
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.010
Then you'll build mesons, which
pair one quark with one antiquark,

10
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.520
like the pions.

11
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.720
Your mission: explain why only
the proton carries a charge.
